extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 18: Mystic Russia pp.83-91. The class id is `necromancer-russian` because this is the RUSSIAN Death Mage; the book distinguishes it from a non-Russian Death Mage explicitly, giving that one three extra Necro-spells in place of Bone Magic. THE TWO STARTING SPELL GROUPS ARE DELIBERATELY SHAPED DIFFERENTLY. The book gives six necromancy spells ''regardless of level'' and six common/wizard spells; `spell_traditions_allowed` is CLASS-WIDE and identical for every group, so naming the bone tradition there would let the six common picks reach Bone Magic too. A named list wins over the tradition gate, so the necromancy six are drawn from an explicit `spell_lists.bone` naming all 59 rows - which also honours ''regardless of level'', since the list replaces the level gate. The common six keep an ordinary level range and therefore see general invocations only. Four skill names needed the catalog''s spelling: the book''s ''Lore: Monsters & Demons'' is Lore: Demons & Monsters, its ''Skin and Prepare Animal Hides & Bones'' is Skin & Prepare Animal Hides (the bones half has no row and is what Bone Magic is for), its ''Pilot Hover Craft'' is Hover Craft (ground), and ''Basic Math'' is Mathematics: Basic. The Horror Factor the character projects and the +2 to save vs Necromancy spells are both in special_abilities rather than bonuses: the first is not a save the character makes, and the schema holds no per-tradition magic save. The secondary skill schedule is EMPTY because the book states a starting six and no per-level additions, which is a stated absence rather than an omission."
