# Necromancer

## Lore

The Necromancer, or Death Mage, practises the magic of the dead - drawing power
from corpses, bone and the moment of dying. In Russia the branch called Bone
Magic is especially common: the enchantment of bones with magical properties,
and their use as building material.

Even the less extreme and better-intentioned Death Mages radiate a Horror
Factor. The work marks them, and most people can feel it before they can say
why.

## Alignment

Selfish or evil, and most are evil. The book notes that most Necromancers are of
anarchist or evil alignment.

## GM Notes

This is the Russian Death Mage. The book draws an explicit line between it and a
non-Russian one: the Russian starts with a fundamental knowledge of Bone Magic
and two specific bone items, while a non-Russian Death Mage takes three
additional Necro-spells instead.

Its tradition does not level-gate: additional necromancy spells and rituals can
be learned or purchased at any time, regardless of experience level.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'necromancer-russian');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'necromancer-russian';

